Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=('a4e5acbcf378fe27212aa011f0f15c3dbedfa9b349313bcd48d4e53953aae252',), event=Revised(decision='lensplanning', at=datetime(2026, 11, 6, 0, 0, 0), actor='owner', title='Before code, write how named experts working together would tackle the change, then build to it', body='Every change starts with a design note at the top of its pull request: imagine the people the brief names, together with the standing roster, working together on this change, and write down how they would tackle it. The standing roster: Alexis King (make invalid states unrepresentable; parse, do not validate), Justin Le (types and functor combinators that compose), Conal Elliott (denotational design: say precisely what a thing means, then derive the implementation from that meaning), Edward Kmett (one general combinator with laws), Evan Czaplicki (the Elm architecture: one model, one update, a view of values), the Rust maintainers (idiom and API), and the git and Pijul maintainers (stores and history). The note says what the change means, its types, the one general piece, what they would delete, and the order of the work. The code is built to the note, and the pull request says where it departed and why. The result is reviewed through the same eyes. A lens that only reviews finds problems too late to change the design.', rationale='The owner, 2026-11-06: ask whether this is how that person would have written the code and plan the changes around it; for example, imagine they worked together on the change, write down how they would tackle it, and write the pull request from that. The owner named Justin Le, Alexis King and Conal Elliott.', supersedes=()))